          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.09,
            0.371,
            0.112
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Sierpinski Gasket"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.113,
            0.848,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "Sierpinski came up with another fractal made in a similar way. An equilateral triangle is broken up into 4 identical equilateral triangles by joining the midpoints of the bigger triangle, and then the central triangle is removed. This procedure is repeated on the 3 remaining triangles, and so on."
        },
        {
